-- title:
--   Closedness of T(K)N(A_K) in GL₂(A_K)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$ and adele ring $\mathbb{A}_K =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K`, and let `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 K) K` denote $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, the general linear group of $2\times 2$ matrices over $\mathbb{A}_K$, carrying its topology as the unit group of the matrix ring. Inside this group consider the subgroup `rationalTorusUnipotent K`, defined as the join (that is, the subgroup generated by the union) of `rationalTorus K` and `adelicUnipotent K`, where `rationalTorus K` is itself the join of the subgroups `rationalCentre K` and `rationalDiagOne K`, and `adelicUnipotent K` is the image of the group homomorphism `unipotentGL2Hom` over $\mathbb{A}_K$, so that the whole subgroup is generated by the rational central, rational rank-one diagonal and adelic unipotent elements. The assertion is that the underlying subset of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ of this subgroup is closed.
--
--   This is the closedness of the group $T(K)N(\mathbb{A}_K)$ of rational-torus times adelic-unipotent elements in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, a consequence of the discreteness of the principal adeles: the proof cites [`NumberField.AdeleRing.finite_setOf_algebraMap_mem_of_isCompact`](thm.html#NumberField.AdeleRing.finite_setOf_algebraMap_mem_of_isCompact), the finiteness of the set of elements of $K$ whose principal adele lies in a given compact subset of $\mathbb{A}_K$. It is used wherever the quotient of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ by this subgroup and its invariant measure are needed, in particular in the estimates for pseudo-Eisenstein series and for class sums.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_isClosed_rationalTorusUnipotent.lean

